SUMMARY: Applications Open for Indiana University’s 2027 Rural Placemakin
 g Studio
DESCRIPTION:Indiana University is accepting applications for the 2027 Rur
 al Placemaking Studio https://news.iu.edu/rural/live/news/53933-rural-com
 munities-invited-to-apply-for-indiana \, a program that connects IU facul
 ty\, staff and students with rural residents to develop ideas for more we
 lcoming\, useful and meaningful public spaces.\n\nIt is a partnership bet
 ween the IU ServeDesign Center at the Eskenazi School of Art\, Architectu
 re + Design and the IU Center for Rural Engagement\, supporting early-sta
 ge planning and design for projects like public spaces\, public art\, way
 finding\, visual communications and pre-architectural planning.\n\nProjec
 ts must be in a publicly accessible space in a rural Indiana community of
  50\,000 people or fewer\, and should be backed by a local partner such a
 s a municipality\, Main Street organization\, volunteer network or reside
 nt committee. Nonprofit status and design experience aren’t required\, an
 d neither is a construction-ready project. The program looks for communit
 ies with a clear vision\, a commitment to community engagement and a plan
  for building on local assets.\n\nSelected communities will take part in 
 planning sessions and design development\, with orientation and site visi
 ts from March through May 2027\, followed by a design period from June 1 
 through August 13. The program does not provide direct project funding\, 
 so participating communities will need to secure resources for materials\
 , installation and implementation.\n\nApplications are open October 9 thr
 ough November 20\, 2026. Applicants can get help through virtual open off
 ice hours on October 15 and November 12\, or an application workshop on N
 ovember 6 from 10:30 AM - 12:00 PM. Learn more and apply here https://new
 s.iu.edu/rural/live/news/53933-rural-communities-invited-to-apply-for-ind
 iana .
CATEGORIES:
