SUMMARY: Dersu Uzala | Michael A. McRobbie's Choice
DESCRIPTION:Epic in form\, intimate in scope\, and set in the forests of 
 Eastern Siberia at the turn of the century\, Dersu Uzala is a moving stor
 y of the friendship that grows between an aging hunter and a Russian surv
 eyor. Based on a memoir by renowned Russian explorer Vladimir Klavdiyevic
 h Arsenyev\, Kurosawa's romantic hymn to nature and the human spirit is p
 erhaps the most persuasive argument for the immense power of nature and t
 he beauty found in simplicity. [142 min\; adventure\, drama\; Russian and
  Mandarin with English subtitles]
