SUMMARY: THURSDAY MUSIC NIGHT: THE HOT CLUB OF BTOWN!
DESCRIPTION:Juniper is thrilled to host an evening of fabulous Jazz Manou
 che with the new quartet\, The Hot Club of Btown! Featured musicians are 
 Steve Mascari\, Ingrid Matthews\, Alan Bent\, and Craig Coley.\n\nA brief
  definition of this genre of music:\n\nJazz manouche is a musical idiom i
 nspired by the Romani jazz guitarist Jean "Django" Reinhardt (1910–1953)\
 , in conjunction with the French jazz violinist Stéphane Grappelli (1908–
 1997)\, as expressed by their group the Quintette du Hot Club de France. 
 The style has its origins in France and the Manouche clan of Romanis and 
 has remained popular amongst this clan.\n\nThis is sure to be an evening 
 filled with truly exceptional music that will uplift all in attendance! D
 o not miss this performance!
CATEGORIES:Bloomington,Free,Music
