SUMMARY: Don't Look Now | Friday Night Frights
DESCRIPTION:Adapted from a Daphne du Maurier short story\, Don't Look Now
  follows John (Donald Sutherland) and Christine (Julie Christie)\, still 
 grieving over the accidental death of their daughter\, as they head to Ve
 nice for John's work restoring a church. Soon\, Laura meets two sisters w
 ho claim to be in touch with the spirit of their dead daughter and the co
 uple must decide what is real\, what is supernatural\, and what is somewh
 ere in-between. Renowned for innovative editing style\, memorable recurri
 ng aesthetic motifs\, an impressionistic formal style\, and nonlinear sto
 rytelling that destabilizes the viewer\, the film was controversial on it
 s release but is now considered a classic\, landing multiples times on Si
 ght and Sound’s list of the best films of all time\, the BFI list of grea
 test British films\, and was reevaluated by Roget Ebert as an occult-horr
 or classic. Don’t Look Now has also inspired filmmakers like Danny Boyle\
 , Lynne Ramsey\, Ari Aster\, Steven Soderbergh\, and many more. [110 min\
 ; horror\; English and Italian]
CATEGORIES:
