SUMMARY: Naza | Additional Films and Guests
DESCRIPTION:Oscar-winning documentarians Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor sp
 ent three years investigating the technological systems inherent to moder
 n warfare\, uncovering their inner workings from the people who designed 
 them. Through interviews with two dozen intelligence officers and soldier
 s\, the film unfolds how civilian causalities are increasing as warfare b
 ecomes increasingly technologized and AI-assisted. While the revelations 
 uncovered during the film were published in real-time by The Guardian and
  other outlets over the last three years\, the film's power lies in the u
 nvarnished testimony of its participants\, letting their own words contex
 tualize their decisions. Winner of the Special Jury Prize at the 83rd Ven
 ice International Film Festival. [80 min\; documentary\; Hebrew with Engl
 ish subtitles]
