SUMMARY: Everybody to Kenmure Street | Arthouse Now
DESCRIPTION:The first day of Eid in Glasgow started as any other. But soo
 n\, neighbors heard through community message networks that two local men
  were snatched up for deportation\, and suddenly hundreds of people left 
 their breakfast tables\, work Zoom calls\, and daily lives to rush down t
 o Kenmure Street to save them by putting their bodies on the line. Though
  mostly strangers\, and with almost no planning\, this extremely diverse 
 group organized themselves\, taking on essential roles to allow the colle
 ctive to protect their own from government forces targeting their least p
 rotected neighbors. An inspiring and profoundly moving portrait of what w
 e all are capable of in the face of injustice\, Everybody to Kenmure Stre
 et reminds us of the power that is always inherent in the people. Winner\
 , World Cinema Documentary Special Jury Award for Civil Resistance\, Sund
 ance Film Festival 2026. [95 min\; documentary\; English]
CATEGORIES:
