SUMMARY: Two Tales of Terror: J-Horror Unleashed with Best Wishes to All/
 Mina Ni Ko Are + Gozu | Friday Night Frights
DESCRIPTION:Best Wishes to All/Mina ni ko are (Yûta Shimotsu\, Japan\, 20
 23): A young woman's visit to her grandparents' home leads to the discove
 ry of what's brought them happiness\, a revelation that will lead her to 
 question her choices\, sanity\, and reality itself. [89 min\; horror\; Ja
 panese with English subtitles]\n\nGozu (Takashi Miike\, Japan\, 2003): Ac
 claimed director Takashi Miike's unhinged Yakuza/horror film continues to
  shock and amaze audiences decades after its original release. Minami is 
 sent to kill his mentor Ozaki (who is in the midst of a nervous breakdown
 ) but soon finds the simple hit quickly morphs into a terrifying and visc
 eral journey into the unexplained and unknown. One of the films in Miike'
 s oeuvre that continues to confound and haunt audiences\, which is saying
  something! [129 min\; horror\; Japanese with English subtitles]
