SUMMARY: Writers Guild First Sunday Prose Reading Series in November
DESCRIPTION:First Sunday Prose in November will feature writers Shana Rit
 ter and Angela Herrmann. It will be a rich afternoon! Come early to sign 
 up for open mic and to find what you’ve always wanted at the Juniper Art 
 Gallery! Sunday\, Nov. 1 4-5:30pm\, 615 W. Kirkwood. Some parking in the 
 back!\n\nS https://writersguildbloomington.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10
 /Shana.jpg hana Ritter writes poetry and prose and pieces in between. Her
  chapbook\, Stairs of Separation was published by Finishing Line Press. I
 n the Time of Leaving\, a novel of exile and resilience\, is set in late 
 15th century Spain. Shana has been awarded the Indiana Individual Artist 
 Grant on multiple occasions.\n\nAngela Herrmann is a writer\, photographe
 r\, teacher\, community scientist\,\nand avid outdoors woman. Her publish
 ing credits include Branches\; Farm\nIndiana\; The Indianapolis Anthology
 \; Literary Hub\; New Teacher Advocate\;\nNUVO\; Outdoor Indiana\; So It 
 Goes The Literary Journal of the Kurt\nVonnegut Museum\; and other public
 ations. She has taught writing and\nEnglish in California\, Indiana\, Chi
 na\, and England. When not writing\,\nshe’s probably outside cycling\, pa
 ddling\, hiking\, or digging around in a\ncommunity garden.
CATEGORIES:Free,Literary-Arts,In-Person
