SUMMARY: Ran/Chaos | Michael A. McRobbie's Choice
DESCRIPTION:After years of consolidating his empire\, the elderly Great L
 ord Hidetora Ichimonji decides to abdicate and divide his domain amongst 
 his three sons. The eldest\, Taro\, will rule\, and his second and third 
 sons—Jiro and Saburo—will take command of his second and third castles\, 
 but are expected to obey their eldest brother. When Sabura is banished fo
 r disobedience\, the (literal) Shakespearean dramatics play out in Kurosa
 wa’s third adaptation of the Bard. Widely considered one of the greatest 
 films ever made and among Kurosawa’s finest filmmaking achievements\, Ran
  continues to set the bar in formally inventive and meticulously crafted 
 adaptive storytelling. [160 min\; tragedy\, drama\, war\; Japanese with E
 nglish subtitles]
CATEGORIES:Free
