SUMMARY: First Thursday Declaration of Independence Lecture
DESCRIPTION:IU Libraries Lilly Library invites you to a special First Thu
 rsday talk in conjunction with our Declaration of Independence exhibition
 s.\n\nAs part of our yearlong America 250 programming\, IU Associate Prof
 essor of History Konstantin Dierks will give a talk entitled “Resonances 
 of the Declaration of Independence in American History.”\n\nIs it worth c
 ommemorating the Declaration of Independence in 2026? Does the Declaratio
 n still have resonance in our time of terrible crisis? The Declaration ex
 pressed ideals with intensely contested and severely limited meanings in 
 1776. Yet those brittle ideals somehow carried forward through American h
 istory. Looking closely at the complexities of 1776 can help us ponder ho
 w the Declaration might speak to our crisis in 2026.\n\nBefore and after 
 the talk\, please feel free to peruse our Declaration of Independence exh
 ibitions: The Motives\, The Moment and The Signers.\n\nThis event is free
 . Please register at this link: First Thursday Declaration of Independenc
 e Lecture / Events Calendar https://events.iu.edu/event/first-thursday-de
 claration
CATEGORIES:
