SUMMARY: Vindication Swim w/ Q&A | Additional Films and Guests
DESCRIPTION:Vindication Swim tells the remarkable story of Mercedes Gleit
 ze\, who in 1927 became the first British woman to swim the English Chann
 el. Facing press hostility\, anti-immigrant bias\, and constraints on wom
 en in sport\, Mercedes’ achievement remains a powerful testament to her g
 rit\, courage\, and determination. Writer-director Elliott Hasler—only 23
  when the film premiered—pursued period authenticity through grassroots c
 ollaboration with coastal communities throughout the UK. Three years in t
 he making\, the film’s swimming sequences were shot miles out in the Chan
 nel\, vividly capturing the perils of Mercedes’ epic crossing. [98 min\; 
 drama\; English]\n\nA Q&A with director Elliott Hasler and Radhika Parame
 swaran (Herman B Wells Endowed Professor\, Media School) will follow the 
 screening.
CATEGORIES:Free
