SUMMARY: Beauty and the Beast (1978) | Underground Film Series
DESCRIPTION:The most uncanny and fierce adaptation of Beauty and the Beas
 t\, the film follows the innocent Julie and her experiences living under 
 the watchful eye of Netvor\, a bird-like being torn between his growing a
 ffection for her and his animalistic urge to kill. Directed by Juraj Herz
  of the Czech New Wave\, Herz masterfully infuses the 18th-century French
  fairytale of impossible affection with the aesthetics of gothic horror. 
 Restored by Národní filmový archiv\, Prague and Severin Films\, supported
  by The Czech Audiovisual Fund. [91 min\; horror\, fantasy\; Czech with E
 nglish subtitles]
CATEGORIES:Free
