SUMMARY: The Ballad of Suzanne Cesaire | New Americas Cinema
DESCRIPTION:Based on the life of writer and feminist activist Suzanne Cés
 aire\, Madeleine Hunt-Ehrlich’s debut feature explores the relationships 
 with Césaire’s husband\, French politician Aimé Césaire\, and fellow surr
 ealist André Breton. Shimmering with the radiance of its Caribbean landsc
 ape and a phenomenal performance from Zita Hanrot\, the film breaks from 
 traditional biographical structure\, blending more conventional narrative
  with captivating experimental elements. [75 min\; biography\, drama\; En
 glish and French with English subtitles]
