SUMMARY: Tokyo Godfathers (2003)
DESCRIPTION:For those who love the BCT’s Studio Ghibli series!\n\nTokyo G
 odfathers is a 2003 Japanese animated Christmas tragicomedy adventure fil
 m written and directed by Satoshi Kon.\n\nOne Christmas Eve\, three homel
 ess people—middle-aged alcoholic Gin\, transgender woman Hana\, and teena
 ge runaway Miyuki—discover an abandoned newborn while searching through t
 he garbage\, along with a note asking whoever finds the baby to take good
  care of her and a key leading to a locker containing a bag holding clues
  to the parents’ identity. The trio sets out to find the baby’s parents\,
  and Hana names her Kiyoko\, after the Japanese title of “Silent Night\,”
  meaning “pure child”.\n\nRated: PG-13\nLength: 1hr 32mins\nFormat: DCP
CATEGORIES:Film,Bloomington
