SUMMARY: The Great Arch | Arthouse Now
DESCRIPTION:1983. French President Mitterrand decides to launch an intern
 ational architectural competition for the flagship project of his mandate
 : the Great Arch of La Défense\, aligned with the Louvre and the Arc de T
 riomphe. Against all odds\, Otto von Spreckelsen\, a Danish architect\, w
 ins the competition. Overnight\, this 53-year-old man\, unknown in France
 \, arrives in Paris where he is propelled to the helm of this pharaonic p
 roject. While the architect intends to build the Great Arch exactly as he
  envisioned\, his ideas quickly clash with realistic constraints and the 
 vicissitudes of politics. [104 min\; drama\; English\, French\, and Dutch
  with English subtitles]
