SUMMARY: Science of Art: Glass Working
DESCRIPTION:WonderLab is teaming up with the Bloomington Creative Glass C
 enter for Science of Art: Glass Working — and things are about to get hot
 .\n\nGlass has a secret double life: it cuts\, melts\, and moves in ways 
 that seem almost magical (spoiler: it's all science). Get hands-on with a
 ctivities for all ages — try your hand at glass fusing\, create a mosaic 
 to take home\, or discover the surprising\, sweet-toothed properties glas
 s shares with sugar.\n\nActivities:\n\nGlass Fusing\n\n  * Make a Heart\,
  Take a Heart —a fun twist on the usual take-home project. Make an unfini
 shed glass heart to leave behind\, then choose a finished one — made by a
  previous visitor — to take home instead. Your piece then heads to BCGC t
 o be finished\, ready for the next person to discover. It's a little chai
 n of glass-making that keeps going\, visitor to visitor\, round after rou
 nd.\n  * Larger Projects — more involved\, creative pieces for older chil
 dren and adults\; pieces are finished off-site by BCGC and available for 
 pickup at their studio. Limited availability.\n\nMosaics\n\n  * Glass Sco
 ring Station (ages 8+) — try your hand at the scoring techniques used in 
 glasswork\n  * Bottlecap & Jar Lid Mosaics — make your own mini mosaic to
  take home as a pin\, magnet\, or ornament.\n\nJolly Rancher Fusion / Sun
 catcher\n\n  * Use real fused-glass techniques on Jolly Rancher shards to
  create edible art.
CATEGORIES:
