SUMMARY: Penguin Cafe
DESCRIPTION:The music of Penguin Cafe Orchestra has permeated popular cul
 ture\, appearing in films (Napoleon Dynamite\, The Founder\, Mary and Max
 )\, television (The Handmaid’s Tale\, Malcolm in the Middle)\, and countl
 ess advertisements. “Music for a Found Harmonium” became a folk-dance sta
 ple\, having been featured on the original iconic Cafe Del Mar album\, an
 d “Perpetuum Mobile” provided the musical foundation for Avicii’s “Fade I
 nto Darkness.”\n\nPenguin Cafe was founded by Arthur Jeffes in 2009\, bri
 nging together a talented and disparate group of musicians initially to p
 erform his father Simon Jeffes’ legacy of world-renowned Penguin Cafe Orc
 hestra music\, ten years after his untimely death in 1997.\n\nSince that 
 time\, Penguin Cafe has continued with Arthur creating new music in the P
 CO tradition of genre-blending\, pastoral soundscapes\, combining classic
 al instruments like violins and cellos with unexpected elements like ukul
 eles and melodicas. The end result is music and performances filled with 
 great joy and beauty that leaves the audience humming the tunes and wanti
 ng for more. They are known for a quintessentially English\, genre-defyin
 g mix of avant-pop\, minimalist classical\, and folk influences.\n\nPengu
 in Cafe have released five studio albums of original music\, four of whic
 h are released on Erased Tapes Records:\n\nA Matter of Life 2008 |The Red
  Book 2014 |The Imperfect Sea 2017 | Handfuls of Night 2019 | Rain Before
  Seven 2023
CATEGORIES:Bloomington,In-Person,Live,Music
